# e2e flow/contract tier secrets — see docs/e2e/README.md §8 and
# .claude/commands/e2e.md. List every auth-shaped env key this project's
# e2e stand needs; a value of GENERATE gets a fresh random token from
# `make e2e-secrets`. Any other value is copied through as-is — use that
# for fixed, non-secret test config, not real credentials.
#
# WATCH OUT: if your e2e compose overlay keeps a database volume warm
# across runs (recommended — a full up/down per test costs minutes), do
# NOT mark that DB's password GENERATE. The password gets baked into the
# data directory once, at first boot; regenerating it on every run while
# the volume survives breaks every service's connection the moment the
# container restarts without a matching `down -v`. Use a fixed value for
# anything baked into a warm volume — GENERATE only for auth tokens
# services re-read from the environment on every boot.
#
# Fill this in as part of the /e2e interview, alongside .e2e/profile.yml.
#
# YOUR_SERVICE_TOKEN=GENERATE
